    </div>

    <p class="prose">
      The top of the leaderboard is a <strong>three-way tie at four wins</strong> &mdash; held by John Barry, John Williams, and Ludwig G&ouml;ransson. Barry's wins span from 1966 to 1990, a 24-year reign that bridges the Silver and Modern eras. Williams' four victories cluster between 1975 and 1993, anchored to the blockbuster era he helped define. G&ouml;ransson's four wins arrive in a compressed burst between 2018 and 2026, making him the fastest composer ever to reach that mark. Below the summit, four composers share three wins each, and ten share two.
    </p>

    <p class="footnote">Note: For multi-composer wins (e.g., 1974, 2010, 2020), each individual is credited with a win. The dataset records Oppenheimer as the winning film in both 2023 and 2024; both entries are counted as given in the source data.</p>
